  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 4.8,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.97,
    "rationale": "Undiluted readings flatten abruptly at ~1.3 from 7 h onward, after a steep exponential rise, which looks like the detector saturating rather than true stationary phase. Dilution tests of the retained aliquots: 18 h at 10x gave 0.4773 and 0.4780, i.e. ~4.78 after correction; 18 h at 20x gave 0.2424, i.e. 4.85. The two dilutions agree, so the reader responds proportionally at these lower ODs, and the true OD at 18 h is about 4.8, roughly 3.6 times the undiluted reading of 1.32. The 12 h aliquot at 10x gave 0.4636, i.e. ~4.64, so the late-phase biomass is also well above the plateau reading. As a check on reader linearity at low OD, the 5 h aliquot at 10x gave 0.0365, i.e. ~0.37, close to its undiluted reading of 0.384. So undiluted readings are reliable at low OD but cap at ~1.3. The late-phase biomass is much higher than the undiluted readings indicate."
  },
